{
  "id": "28814_doraggu",
  "headword": "ドラッグ",
  "reading": "どらっぐ",
  "romaji": "doraggu",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "drag (computing); dragging with mouse or finger",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "drag (computing); dragging an item with mouse or finger",
      "explanation": "The action of holding down a button or touching a screen and moving an item across the display. Used for moving files, scrolling, selecting text, or operating on-screen objects."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28814_doraggu_ex1",
      "japanese": "アイコンをドラッグした。",
      "english": "I dragged the icon.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28814_doraggu_ex2",
      "japanese": "ファイルをフォルダにドラッグして{移動|いどう}する。",
      "english": "Drag the file to the folder to move it.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28814_doraggu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{画面|がめん}を{下|した}にドラッグすると、{次|つぎ}のページが{表示|ひょうじ}される。",
      "english": "If you drag the screen downward, the next page is displayed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "From English 'drag'. Used as a noun and frequently with する (ドラッグする) as a verb. Distinct from the homophone ドラッグ meaning 'drug', which is usually contextually unambiguous.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ドラッグする: to drag\n- ドラッグ＆ドロップ: drag and drop\n- マウスでドラッグする: to drag with the mouse\n- {画面|がめん}をドラッグする: to drag the screen\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- スワイプ: swipe — a quick touchscreen flick, typically without holding\n- スクロール: scroll — moves the view, not an object",
